This is the "about once a month" note from when you signed up.

One thing worth doing if you will see your parent over Thanksgiving: spend
ten minutes on what a phone call can't show you. Set their pill bottles out
next to the medication list you have and look for three things: a bottle
that isn't on the list, two bottles of the same medicine from different
pharmacies or doctors, and old bottles that should have gone. If anything
looks off, take a photo and ask their pharmacist, who will check it for
free. While you're there, ring their phone from the room they sit in most
and make sure they can hear it.

What has changed since last month: if your parent doesn't answer, Remindly
can now ring you. For a reminder where being late matters, if none of the
calls to your parent is answered, Remindly phones the family one at a time,
in the order you choose, until someone presses 1 to say they'll check, and
emails everyone else to say who's on it:

<%= ApplicationHelper::CANONICAL_HOST %>/faq?from=monthly-note#if-they-still-dont-answer

And if you'd rather not set it up alone, book a free 15-minute call and
we'll do it with you on the phone: your parent, their first reminder, and
what they'll hear.

